{
  "unit": "text_oneshot__PMC11355469__broad",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Wear resistance initially increases as ambient temperature rises to a critical threshold.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial increase in wear resistance is driven by formation of a protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tribological performance degrades sharply above the critical temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature degradation is caused by thermo-plastic instability and loss of oxide-layer structural integrity.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4976365::chunk::000::abstract::c056d652e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "AlCoCrFeNiTi0.5 can have a fine microstructure containing two BCC phases and an additional complex phase after processing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HEA coatings or films can be produced by laser cladding or sputter deposition and can possess high hardness suitable for wear-resistant applications.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::chunk::001::introduction::c558c6fff9"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing temperature causes a transition from dislocation-mediated plasticity to thermo-plastic instability in the HEA matrix.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4976365::chunk::000::abstract::c056d652e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At moderate temperatures, the coefficient of friction decreases with increasing temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The thermally formed oxide layer is dense and adherent and acts as both a solid lubricant and a barrier to abrasive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::chunk::000::abstract::cd6baea278"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Higher temperature and stress can promote atomistic rearrangements and a clustering-to-ordering transition in an Al-Cr-Co-Fe-Ni HEA.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC4976365::chunk::000::abstract::c056d652e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermally induced rearrangement or loss of short-range order softens the HEA matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Matrix softening causes spallation of the protective oxide layer and accelerates wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Specific wear rate reaches a minimum at approximately 400-600 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Above the peak-performance temperature, wear rate increases exponentially.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At sufficiently high temperature, wear rate eventually exceeds its room-temperature value.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "For many HEAs, degradation likely begins above approximately 600-700 °C when the protective oxide exceeds its thermal stability limit.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermo-plastic instability causes loss of cocktail-effect hardening.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The transition temperature depends on HEA composition, including the presence of Al, Cr, W, or Mo.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7475834::chunk::001::introduction::97cd4ea6cb",
        "PMC4976365::chunk::000::abstract::c056d652e0"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The transition temperature depends on sliding load and speed.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermo-plastic instability is known to dominate above 800 °C for the proposed specific alloy.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
